Notes for the send:

- `dedupe_contacts` keeps opted-out people and marks them `opted_out="Y"`, so filter them out before sending: `recipients = [p for p in dedupe_contacts(rows) if p["opted_out"] == "N"]`.
- If any `updated` value doesn't match one of the three formats, the function raises `ValueError` rather than guessing. That's deliberate, so a bad export gets caught before the send.
- I applied the ZIP+4 rule only to the strict `12345-6789` form. Something like `2139-4307` becomes `""`. Tell me if your data person meant something looser.
